# The handover lives in GitLab issue #157; the session-start hook saves its last copy here for when
# GitLab is down. The old in-repo handover stays ignored so an older branch's copy is never re-added.
.claude/handover.cache.md*
.claude/active_work.md

# site_v2 per-entity export build artifact (#365)
artifacts/site_data/

# Design-mock OUTPUT. The generators and their checks are tracked (they read the metric catalogue
# and system.css, so they must version with what they read); the HTML they render is build output,
# ~950 KB of it, and is regenerated by `python design-mocks/gen_*.py`.
design-mocks/*.html
design-mocks/__pycache__/
design-mocks/_astro/

# site_v2 real-data build: the site build enumerates src/data/{teams,fixtures}/*.json. Only the
# committed samples are tracked; a full export populates these dirs at build time (100s MB to >1 GB)
# and must never be committed. Keep the samples, ignore the bulk.
#
# THE SAMPLE SET MUST BE SELF-CONSISTENT (#367). The landing page links to the next matchday,
# and `audit-seo.mjs` fails the build on any internal link that does not resolve to an emitted page.
# So every entity the committed `landing.json` points at needs its payload here, or CI goes red
# while a local build with a full export stays green -- which is exactly the trap this list sprang
# the first time. ~1.7 MB total: samples, not bulk.
#
# Six team payloads (132, 463, 587, 1607, 2242, 2759) were tracked here until the trending block was
# cut on 2026-08-08. They were listed ONLY because trending rows linked to them; with that block
# gone nothing on the site linked to a team page, so they emitted six orphans. 33.json stays -- it is
# the team-page's own sample and predates the landing work.
# ⚠ THAT LAST SENTENCE STOPPED BEING TRUE ON 2026-09-09. The Home Top teams block (#41) links every
# row to a team page, so 20 payloads are tracked again below -- for the same reason the six were
# once tracked, and the same reason the fixtures are. The orphan problem was the block being cut,
# never the linking itself.
#
# ⚠ REGENERATE AS A SET. `landing.json` is a snapshot of whatever fixtures are next, so refreshing
# it changes WHICH ids belong below. Refresh the landing sample and these entries together, or the
# next build fails on links to ids that are no longer here.
# Export byproducts: `export_site_data.py` writes both into its output dir on every run. Neither is
# part of the tracked sample, and both turned up as untracked strays the first time this sample was
# refreshed from a full export. Ignored rather than deleted, so the next refresh does not re-arm the
# same stray-file gate.
site_v2/src/data/manifest.json
site_v2/src/data/slug_map.json
site_v2/src/data/teams/*.json
# The teams the Home Top teams boards link to (#41: "Every row links out. That is why the block
# exists."). Same rule as the fixtures block below and for the same reason: landing.json links to
# these pages, and those pages exist only if the payload behind each one is committed — audit-seo
# check 8 fails the build otherwise. 33 (Manchester United) predates the block as the team-page
# sample and is kept.
#
# ⚠ REGENERATE AS A SET. The boards change with the data, so a refresh changes WHICH team ids belong
# here. Re-export, rewrite this list to exactly the ids the new landing.json links, `git rm` the
# ones that left, all in the same commit — a stale entry pins a payload nothing re-exports.
!site_v2/src/data/teams/33.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/49.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/50.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/51.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/55.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/85.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/106.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/157.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/194.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/209.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/211.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/224.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/420.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/505.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/529.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/536.json
!site_v2/src/data/teams/867.json
# The 18 clubs of the Bundesliga table on the committed competition page sample (GitLab #149):
# every table row and deserved-points row links to its team page. 157 is listed above.
!site_v2/src/data/teams/182.json
